# Collection model

Unit of collection = one screenshot (`specimen`) with independent tags. Never store a combo name as a tag (`shadow_shiny_polos`). Combos are categories.

Visual uniqueness key: `species + form + shiny + costume + shadowStatus + background + custom tags`. IV is not in that key. "Normal IV" is not a tag.

A **category** is a name plus a set of required tags the user picks. Seed defaults (Basic, Shiny, Shadow, Purified, Costume, Background, Hundo, Nundo). Users may add more.

- Basic = no required tags. Pure = specimen with zero tags (default look).
- A custom category saved with **no picked tags** (Lucky, etc.) defines one new atomic tag from its name. That tag shows in required tags and on Transfer.
- Picking existing tags makes a combo track (`[shadow, hundo]`). Do not store a combo name as a tag (`shadow_shiny_polos`).
- Shadow polos = category tags `[shadow]` only. Do not add an IV tag unless the category is meant to be Shadow Hundo / Shadow Nundo.
- Hundo / Nundo are optional tags (`hundo`, `nundo`), not a generic `iv` tag.

A species is **in** a category if some specimen's tags include every required tag (extras allowed).

```text
# Category "Shadow" required: [shadow]
# gray: [shadow, shiny, tokyo]
# green: [shadow]

# Category "Shadow Hundo" required: [shadow, hundo]
# green only when tags are exactly [shadow, hundo]
```
